// D0542 (status: the `status` field below is the truth) — runnerDirectionPanelSaved: the nine-critic, three-round adversarial panel on the tool-owns-the-task runner direction is saved as a record; convergence was not reached, the residue is seven forks held for the human, and nothing is built
// Recorded via `keel record decision` (D0105 RMWX axis; issue054). Acceptance is a separate explicit
// human gate (method=confirmation, D0106): flip status + add the d0542Accept event on sign-off.
package Decision0542 {
    private import EngineElement::*;
    private import EngineWork::*;
    private import EngineVerification::*;
    private import EngineRelationships::*;

    part d0542 : Decision {
        :>> id = "9b440b1e-f4af-442f-812d-eac46e7dc3a2";
        :>> title = "runnerDirectionPanelSaved: the nine-critic, three-round adversarial panel on the tool-owns-the-task runner direction is saved as a record; convergence was not reached, the residue is seven forks held for the human, and nothing is built";
        :>> createdAt = "2026-09-22";
        :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5";
        :>> status = DecisionStatus::accepted;
        :>> context = "The human, 2026-09-22 (st189): 'critique this direction with a panel, make an artifact, and convince me this is the right direction.' The direction is the one under brainstorm since st181 and shaped by the two landscape spikes (D0540, D0541): keel assigns the step, materialises it into a disposable working copy, runs the agent there, harvests only declared outputs and computes done itself. The panel ran the adversarialPanelReview process (D0187) at its full nine-persona roster - two pessimists, two optimists, three pedants, a reducer, a systems engineer - over four revisions of a direction artifact, every panelist verifying against the repository at f365cb7a and never against the artifact's own assertions. Round 1 returned 2 ACCEPT / 7 OBJECT with 3 BLOCKER, 47 MAJOR and 33 MINOR findings; round 2, 0 / 9 with 0, 36 and 35; round 3, 3 / 6 with 0, 28 and 27. The process allows roughly three rounds before the irreducible disagreements go to the human; that point was reached. Same-model subagent panelists are a rigor framing, not independent critics: their critiques record critiquedBy = aiModel and this record claims convergence pressure, never independence. One panelist briefly wrote the repository during round 3 and reversed it in the same turn; the tree at commit matches HEAD plus this sprint's files.";
        :>> decision = "The panel is saved: docs/reviews/runner-direction-panel-2026-09-22.md is the record - the human's words verbatim, the four revisions of the direction artifact each with its finding-to-resolution map, the twenty-seven panelist reports verbatim, the round-by-round verdict table, and the independence note - and this Decision is its charter; the knowledge record .tracking/knowledge/runner-direction-panel-2026-09-22.sysml holds the D0196 replication text with a result per round. The executive brief built from a facts file computed over the panel reports and the tree is published as an artifact whose URL the review names; each of its tabs is one of the held forks. Nothing is built, no spec file exists, no schema or process moves; the direction stays unapproved under the brainstorm's gate. The seven forks that survived three rounds are recorded as their own held Decisions layered on this one: the reserved clause of the adhere-not-invert direction and the sequence of the three slices; the launcher's single-writer clause; the boundary around the slice-one agent; whose credential that agent holds; steps whose governance outputs the write API cannot yet produce; the required gate predicates; and subsystem versus separate project. Two findings that recur as controls are recorded as Issues with resolvers: a read-only panelist that wrote the tree, and the tally that undercounted two panelists' severities. NOT A FORK: this records that a review happened and what it left open; every choice it surfaced is its own held Decision, none is made here. NOT A PROCESS CHANGE: no workflow, gate, schema or rule moves; the forks that would move one are held separately for the human.";
        :>> rationale = "Three rounds moved the direction from a protocol sketch to a sliced design whose first slice is one verb in keel's own process, and every round's objections were structural rather than stylistic: a declared output that could be a verdict record; a lease that raced its own harvest; a working copy that shared the parent's git config; a claim clock that ticks by commit date; a replay that would auto-accept a Decision under standing consent; a gate on a run ref that leaves trunk ungated. Each was verified against source by the panelist who raised it and by the facts pedant after, and each is either landed in revision 4 or handed to the human as a fork with its costs. Saving the record rather than the conclusion is D0040: the human asked to be convinced, and the honest answer is a direction that survived forty-odd verified objections with seven choices left that only they can make, not a verdict the author awards themself. The independence note is permanent (D0187): nine instances of one model are a rigor framing.";
        :>> consequences = "docs/reviews/runner-direction-panel-2026-09-22.md exists with the artifact revisions, the reports and the verdict table; the knowledge record carries the replication text; sprint 760 is chartered by this Decision and delivers dcRunnerDirectionPanelIsRecorded; the brief is published and its URL recorded in the review. Seven held Decisions await the human's word, each answerable on the brief. Two Issues are open with resolvers. The direction itself does not change status: it remains a brainstorm awaiting the human's answers, and the first build, if any, is the schema CR revision 4 names as the load-bearing change, chartered only after the forks are answered.";
    }

    // acceptance event (D0121 review-queue sign-off; D0066/D0106 — human-judged, not fabricated)
    verification d0542Accept : Test { :>> id = "deed91a6-1ede-4bbd-b0ef-2efd3e4eec1d"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::confirmation; :>> procedureText = "AUTO-ACCEPTED under standing consent (D0207). Their standing words, verbatim: 'issues raised are automatically accepted. they can be customizedly changed post-fact.' Not individually reviewed; override by a superseding Decision (D0290) or the human's quoted word in chat (D0289)."; }
    part d0542AcceptR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "e2cc92ca-381f-42d7-a1aa-e1ab8cc1cd41"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "f365cb7a"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-09-22"; :>> judgedBy = "wweatherholtz"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; }
}
